<title>BRAZIL: Brazil gov't sells 74 pct coffee in stock auction.</title>
<headline>Brazil gov't sells 74 pct coffee in stock auction.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's government sold 63,084 60-kg bags of coffee or 73.81 percent of its auction today of 85,466 bags of stocks, said an official from Banco do Brasil which held the electronic auction.</p>
<p>Prices ranged between 88 and 110.50 reais (US$85.44 and $107.28) a bag, the official said.</p>
<p>The next auction is scheduled to be held Dec 18.</p>
<p>--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
